E         +
E         +## 55. Contract Amendment History — Phase 149O.20L.7K (v1.4)
E         +
E         +**Status of this section:** descriptive/historical record of the
E         +149O.20L.7K contract-and-production amendment, appended without
E         +modifying the original v1.0 freeze narrative (§0-48), §49-52's v1.0/
E         +v1.1/v1.2 history, §53's v1.3 amendment, or §54's repair record.
E         +
E         +**Context.** By 149O.20L.7J, the `DeploymentBinding` producer —
E         +`core/hatp_deployment_binding_admin.py` (149O.20L.7I) and its sole
E         +intended Protected Admin ceremony caller `scripts/hatp_deployment_
E         +binding_admin.py` (149O.20L.7I) — was independently verified to
E         +implement HBDC-001 v1.1's create/rotate/revoke ceremony correctly
E         +(HBDC-REQ-056..070), with zero real invocations, entirely outside
E         +HMIC-001's frozen twenty-eight-file identity (7J §31, its own named,
E         +non-blocking-for-HBDC finding). This left that gap open: an edit to
E         +either file could silently change what `DeploymentBinding` the
E         +already-frozen `hatp_bootstrap.py`/`repository_identity.py` read path
E         +accepts as authoritative, and therefore the Class-B deployment-
E         +conformance verdict `hatp_class_b_conformance.py::_check_deployment_
E         +identity` (HBDC-REQ-042) folds into its aggregate, without changing any
E         +digest HMIC-001 already computes. This section records 149O.20L.7K's
E         +independent derivation of the exact closure this gap requires —
E         +contract amendment **and** production alignment in the same phase
E         +(deliberately not split across a contract-then-alignment sequence the
E         +way §53/149O.20K.2/149O.20K.3 were, since this phase's own governing
E         +scope directs a single combined amendment).
E         +
E         +**§55.1 Independent reconstruction of HMIC-REQ-052 (as it stood at
E         +v1.3).** Before analyzing the producer, 149O.20L.7K re-read HMIC-REQ-052
E         +from this document directly (not from 7J's summary). At v1.3, the
E         +closure rule bound a PCAE-owned file only if reachable, transitively,
E         +from: (a) `assess_hatp_mandatory_activation_readiness`'s own call graph;
E         +(b) `validate_active_hatp_mandatory_independent_verification_
E         +certification`'s call graph, or the Protected Admin ceremony functions
E         +`certify`/`activate`/`revoke` in `scripts/hatp_certification_admin.py`;
E         +or (c) `verify_class_b_deployment_conformance`'s own call graph. A
E         +direct text search of `hatp_class_b_conformance.py` (the sole entry
E         +point limb (c) names) confirms it imports `hatp_bootstrap`,
E         +`repository_identity`, the topology/environment-lock verifier modules,
E         +and `pcae.core.paths` only — it does **not** import `core/hatp_
E         +deployment_binding_admin.py`, `scripts/hatp_deployment_binding_
E         +admin.py`, or any symbol from either. None of limbs (a), (b), or (c) as
E         +their v1.3 "specifically, any file reachable from ... call graph" text
E         +literally reads reaches the producer or its admin script: the producer
E         +is a separate write path, never imported by, and never importing, any
E         +v1.3-bound entry point. Under the v1.3 text alone, the two files are
E         +therefore *not* bound by HMIC-REQ-052 — not an oversight in the v1.3
E         +text (it correctly closed what was reachable from the three named call
E         +graphs that existed at v1.3), but a genuine scope gap of a different
E         +shape than §53's: the Class-B verifier island lacked a call-graph
E         +anchor entirely (§53.1); the DeploymentBinding producer has a call-graph
E         +anchor that exists but does not reach it, because the producer
E         +influences the verdict through the *data* it writes, not through being
E         +called by the verifier. This is exactly why limb (c) required a second,
E         +non-reachability anchor (mirroring limb (b)'s own dual-anchor
E         +construction at v1.1, §50) rather than a fourth limb: the concern is the
E         +same verdict limb (c) already names, reached by a different mechanism.
E         +
E         +**§55.2 Independent reconstruction of the current 28/5 identity.** Read
E         +directly from `src/pcae/core/hatp_mandatory_certification.py`, as it
E         +stood immediately before this phase's own production edit:
E         +`_FROZEN_SRC_PCAE_RELATIVE_FILES` (22 entries) + `_FROZEN_REPOSITORY_
E         +ROOT_RELATIVE_FILES` (6 entries, the five bound contract documents plus
E         +`scripts/hatp_certification_admin.py`) = `_FROZEN_AUTHORITY_BEARING_
E         +FILES`, `assert`-pinned at exactly 28 in the module itself. Compared
E         +entry-for-entry against this document's own pre-amendment HMIC-REQ-050
E         +text: identical, in the same order, confirming production and contract
E         +were already in alignment at 28/5 (149O.20K.2/149O.20K.3's own
E         +established result) before this phase. `_CONTRACT_IDENTITY_FILES`
E         +independently read: exactly five `(contract_id, path)` pairs —
E         +`HMRC-001`, `HATP-001`, `HSCE-001`, `RAE-001`, `HBDC-001` — matching
E         +HMIC-REQ-067, unchanged target for this phase (§55.10). Both sets
E         +recorded here as the pre-amendment baseline this phase widens from.
E         +
E         +**§55.3 Fresh static dependency graph — the two producer files.** An
E         +`ast`-based import walk (`ast.parse` + `ast.walk` for `Import`/
E         +`ImportFrom` nodes) was run independently against the current on-disk
E         +bytes of both files, not against 7J's or 7I's prior dependency
E         +narrative. Results:
E         +
E         +- `core/hatp_deployment_binding_admin.py`: `from pcae.core.hatp_
E         +  bootstrap import (DeploymentBinding, HATPTrustStore,
E         +  HATPTrustStoreError, HATPTrustStoreMalformedError,
E         +  HATPTrustStoreSymlinkError, REGISTRY_SCHEMA_VERSION, _parse_registry_
E         +  document, resolve_canonical_deployment_root)`, `from pcae.core.paths
E         +  import HarnessPath`, `from pcae.core.provenance import append_
E         +  provenance_event`, `from pcae.core.repository_identity import
E         +  (RepositoryIdentityError, read_repository_identity)`; everything else
E         +  is standard library (`fcntl`, `json`, `os`, `re`, `tempfile`,
E         +  `contextlib`, `dataclasses`, `datetime`, `enum`, `pathlib`, `typing`).
E         +  No dynamic (`importlib.import_module`/`__import__`) PCAE-owned import
E         +  found by text search of the module.
E         +- `scripts/hatp_deployment_binding_admin.py`: `from pcae.core.hatp_
E         +  bootstrap import HATPTrustStoreError`, `from pcae.core.hatp_
E         +  deployment_binding_admin import (AuthorityEvidence, ..., create_
E         +  deployment_binding, preview_create_deployment_binding, preview_revoke_
E         +  deployment_binding, preview_rotate_deployment_binding, revoke_
E         +  deployment_binding, rotate_deployment_binding)` (the sixteen public
E         +  names the script's `main` dispatches to), `from pcae.core.repository_
E         +  identity import RepositoryIdentityError`; everything else is standard
E         +  library (`argparse`, `sys`, `pathlib`, `typing`).
E         +
E         +No third PCAE-owned module is reached by either file's import
E         +statements beyond the pair being classified, `hatp_bootstrap`, `pcae.
E         +core.paths`, `pcae.core.provenance`, and `repository_identity`.
E         +`hatp_bootstrap` and `repository_identity` are already HMIC-REQ-050
E         +members (§55.2's baseline). `pcae.core.paths` is not — see §55.5, same
E         +disposition as §49/§53. `pcae.core.provenance` is not — see §55.5, a
E         +disposition not previously worked in this contract's history.
E         +
E         +**§55.4 Semantic dependency check and zero-consumer/zero-invocation
E         +confirmation.** Text search of all of `src/` for `hatp_deployment_
E         +binding_admin` (module name) and `create_deployment_binding`/`rotate_
E         +deployment_binding`/`revoke_deployment_binding` (the three producer
E         +entry points), excluding the two files themselves and their own test
E         +modules, returned zero matches: no production module — not `hatp_
E         +bootstrap.py`, not `hatp_class_b_conformance.py`, not `hatp_mandatory_
E         +certification.py`, not `scripts/hatp_certification_admin.py`, not any
E         +readiness/certification/activation/Permission-Broker code — imports or
E         +calls into the producer. `hatp_class_b_conformance.py::_check_
E         +deployment_identity` reads `DeploymentBinding` state via `HATPTrustStore.
E         +load_repository_enrollment`/`hatp_bootstrap.deployment_binding_matches`
E         +(both already-frozen `hatp_bootstrap.py` read primitives) — it does not
E         +call the producer, confirming §55.1's "data dependency, not call-graph
E         +dependency" characterization directly at the source. Separately
E         +reconfirmed (mirroring 7J's own §31/§33): no real `DeploymentBinding`
E         +has ever been created on any host by this producer — every prior test
E         +of it, and every test added by this phase (§55.13), targets disposable
E         +paths only.
E         +
E         +*(Scope note added 149O.20L.7L.1, finding F-7L-1; see §56.1.)* This
E         +section's "zero-consumer" finding is, and was always, scoped to the
E         +`DeploymentBinding` **producer** (`create_deployment_binding`/`rotate_
E         +deployment_binding`/`revoke_deployment_binding` and their admin-ceremony
E         +caller) — it does not establish, and was never evidence for, any claim
E         +about `verify_class_b_deployment_conformance` itself. §55.15 previously
E         +cited this section alongside §53.4 as joint support for a broader "zero
E         +production consumers of `verify_class_b_deployment_conformance`" verdict
E         +sentence; that citation was inaccurate and is repaired at §55.15 and
E         +§56.1 — `verify_class_b_deployment_conformance` already had a real
E         +production readiness/activation consumer (`hatp_mandatory_cutover.py`,
E         +wired by Phase 149O.20L.3) at the time this section was written. The
E         +producer-level finding above is unaffected and remains correct.
E         +
E         +**§55.5 Dependency classification.** Every dependency reached by
E         +§55.3's walk is classified:
E         +
E         +- **Category A (PCAE-owned, authority-sensitive — bind).** The two root
E         +  files themselves. `core/hatp_deployment_binding_admin.py`'s
E         +  `create_deployment_binding`/`rotate_deployment_binding`/`revoke_
E         +  deployment_binding` each independently decide whether a
E         +  `DeploymentBinding` write is `ALREADY_SATISFIED`, a fresh mutation, or
E         +  a fail-closed rejection (`DuplicateConflictingBindingError`/
E         +  `DeploymentBindingNotFoundError`/`DeploymentBindingRevokedError`), and
E         +  what authority-bearing field values (`principal_id`, `signer_key_id`,
E         +  `provider_profile`, `authority_scope`, `canonical_deployment_root`)
E         +  the resulting record carries — a byte edit here (e.g. dropping the
E         +  create-against-revoked fail-closed check, or widening the idempotency
E         +  comparison to ignore `principal_id`) changes what `DeploymentBinding`
E         +  state becomes durably active without changing any pre-v1.4 HMIC-bound
