E         +**§59.19 Certification Record Closed Schema — six-member consequence,
E         +distinct from Wave B's seven-member derivation.** `_CONTRACT_VERSIONS_
E         +REQUIRED_KEYS` (§59.17) is widened by this phase's own two new members
E         +only, to exactly six (`HMRC-001`/`HATP-001`/`HSCE-001`/`RAE-001`/
E         +`HPSE-001`/`HHCE-001`) — the pre-existing `HBDC-001` gap is left
E         +untouched, unchanged from 149O.20L.7O.2G.1's own reconfirmation. The
E         +canonical `CertificationRecord` schema (HMIC-REQ-031/032) therefore
E         +remains deterministic and closed at exactly six required keys as parsed
E         +by `_require_contract_versions`: a valid new record must supply all six;
E         +a record containing only a strict subset is rejected as `MALFORMED`
E         +(missing required key); a record containing a seventh, unrecognized key
E         +— including, still, `HBDC-001` itself, exactly as before this phase —
E         +is rejected as `MALFORMED` (unknown key) — no optional/partial-validity
E         +compatibility behavior is introduced, consistent with HMIC-REQ-031's
E         +pre-existing closed-schema discipline and this contract's own
E         +"no compatibility-mapping table exists" rule (HMIC-REQ-069). This is a
E         +narrower, deliberately incomplete mirror of Wave B's own `derive_
E         +contract_versions`, which correctly returns the full seven-member
E         +mapping (§59.10) — the two mechanisms' divergence over `HBDC-001` is the
E         +same pre-existing, disclosed drift named at §59.17, carried forward
E         +unrepaired by this phase, not a new inconsistency this phase
